 - Add :func:`moabb.analysis.plotting.plot_critical_difference` for comparing pipelines across complete multi-dataset benchmarks with Friedman ranks and Nemenyi critical-difference groups (:gh:`1127` by `lindicaphxag-tech`_).
 - Spell MNE's renamed template montages everywhere: MNE 1.13 renamed ``standard_1005``/``standard_1020`` (and the other ``standard_*`` templates) to ``colin27_*`` (identical electrode files), warns on the old names and MNE 1.14 removes them, so every ``make_standard_montage``/``set_montage`` call in MOABB now spells ``colin27_*``. ``METADATA`` montage labels are descriptive and unchanged (:gh:`1200` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Add :class:`moabb.datasets.Ma2022`, the SHU cross-session motor-imagery dataset: 25 subjects, five sessions, 32 EEG channels at 250 Hz and 11,988 retained 4 s trials. Read the authors' EDF release and BIDS events from NEMAR ``nm000288`` (publication pending), preserving bad-channel flags. These are authors-preprocessed, concatenated imagery windows, not continuous amplifier recordings. The ``Ma-edf2022`` code prevents reuse of legacy MATLAB caches; there is no MATLAB fallback (:gh:`1178` by `LiQing`_ and `Bruno Aristimunha`_)
+- Document how to add a BIDS dataset: the :class:`~moabb.datasets.base.BaseBIDSDataset` docstring now names :class:`moabb.datasets.Zhou2016` as the template subclass and lists the steps, and the dataset-submission section of the data summary links to it (:gh:`726` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
+- Finish moving the BIDS conversion example to the public dataset API: it locates the original files with :meth:`~moabb.datasets.base.BaseDataset.data_path` instead of reading ``MNE_DATA`` and hard-coding the ``MNE-alexeeg-data`` folder, documents the ``format`` and ``overwrite`` options of :meth:`~moabb.datasets.base.BaseDataset.convert_to_bids`, and points to :class:`~moabb.datasets.base.LocalBIDSDataset` for loading the BIDS copy back (:gh:`1082` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
+- Make GitHub's "Cite this repository" export the MOABB software citation as BibTeX ``@misc`` instead of ``@software``, which many bibliography styles drop together with the DOI: ``CITATION.cff`` gains a ``preferred-citation`` of type ``generic`` that reuses the same authors, title, version and DOI, matching the ``@misc`` entries already in the README and :doc:`cite`; the BibTeX block in :doc:`cite` is re-indented with spaces (:gh:`1071` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
+- Explain the default 8-32 Hz band-pass of :class:`moabb.paradigms.MotorImagery` and :class:`moabb.paradigms.LeftRightImagery` in a Notes section: it keeps the mu and beta rhythms, limits muscle and ocular artifacts, and matches the MOABB benchmark, and the section shows how to change it (``fmin``/``fmax``), disable it (``fmin=None, fmax=None``) or use a filter bank. The defaults are unchanged (:gh:`533` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 
